{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/97163-an-alternative-form-of-changeling-governance","id":97163,"title":"An Alternative Form of Changeling Governance.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-23T18:33:55-07:00","id":97163,"title":"An Alternative Form of Changeling Governance.","content":"I'm in a campaign set in Roswell, New Mexico. <br /> There are four (soon to be five) player changelings and two NPCs. We might be up against several prometheans, or aliens, or we might not face any threats at all. We've ruled out forming a motley in favor of creating a structure akin to a freehold, a Changeling Council. Here's about as far as we've gotten with the idea.<br /> <br /> Each member of the council will have their own specialties, abilities, talents, and things they're called upon to perform. The Council will have a meeting at least one a month where major decisions are made. Those will be decided by majority, super-majority, or unanimous vote. There'll also be a head of the Council. The head will keep order, break ties, etc. We're starting off with $50,000.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever heard of or had any experiences with changeling governance that wasn't through the fae or a freehold?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T06:33:19-07:00","id":97484,"title":"","content":"In our game we are sort of in the same boat. We were the only group of Lost in town, so a freehold wasn't really the way to go. We did form a motley, but that was really about us, not the town. We've started making some connections with a freehold in another town, and we've started... meddling in local affairs in the town we are in. Since of our group one has moved (who didn't interact much anyway) and the other constantly bicker and argue with each other my guy was voted leader. An amazingly successful turn of events lead to a sizable number of Lost exiting in the town, and there is hopes of establishing a Freehold. Not exactly what you were going for, but just letting you know you aren't alone with such deviancy from the &quot;norm&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2546-jaellot","name":"jaellot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T09:30:42-07:00","id":97568,"title":"","content":"I know an advantage of belonging to a court is getting to access the court contracts and that not having proper courts as such cuts us off from those contracts, but we wouldn't be able to support a proper system of courts with just 7 people anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T15:11:59-07:00","id":97783,"title":"","content":"While the Changelings in my game do have an established (if small) Freehold, I had them meet Changelings from a neighbouring city with just seven members. Those seven had been able to form a Freehold, with four Spring members, two Summer, and one Autumn. Although they did symbolically follow the changing seasons for the rotation of power (Spring ruling right through Winter and into Spring), they were a small enough group that they tended to settle things democratically.<br /> <br /> I should note that, going by the write-up on the Miami setting, not every season needs to be represented. If I remember right Miami only had three courts when its Freehold was first founded.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I've found it possible to run a &quot;Freehold&quot; of just seven people. It obviously makes the system of governance highly personal, and I've tended to run them more like a school clique than any kind of larger organisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T00:15:00-07:00","id":103244,"title":"","content":"So far we'd have one member of the South Court, a member of the Dawn Court (myself), and one NPC who would be starting his own Space Court. The other PC's are courtless. Going with a conventional court structure isn't an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}